# Everything below is regenerated by one of the scripts documented in
# README.md — none of it needs to be committed, and keeping it out
# avoids tracking large diffs from a rebuild. Each directory keeps a
# .gitkeep placeholder (see the !-exceptions) so the skeleton is still
# visible in a fresh checkout, pointing at the script that fills it in.

# pull_upstream_docs.sh — a real git clone of the upstream end-user
# docs (its own .git and all), so it can't carry a tracked .gitkeep
# placeholder the way the other regenerated directories below do — git
# treats a directory containing its own .git as an embedded repo,
# opaque to this outer repo's normal per-file tracking. The script
# creates this directory itself on first run, so there's no skeleton
# to preserve here anyway.
/upstream-phpbb-documentation/

# convert_dev_docs_to_docbook.sh — pinned pandoc binary cache, and the
# generated English DocBook conversion output. dev-docs-docbook/<lang>/
# for any OTHER language (e.g. dev-docs-docbook/da/, dev-docs-docbook/fr/)
# is NOT generated by any script — see README.md's "Adding another
# language" section — and is deliberately not matched by this pattern,
# so it stays tracked.
/.pandoc-cache/
/dev-docs-docbook/en/*
!/dev-docs-docbook/en/.gitkeep

# phpbbdocs_hugo.sh / phpbbdocs_hugo_devdocs.sh — generated Hugo content and
# build output. config.toml, layouts/, i18n/, and static/css|js/ are
# hand-authored site files and stay tracked; content/, public/,
# resources/, and the copied-in static/<lang>/images/ are all derived.
/site/content/*
!/site/content/.gitkeep
/site/public/*
!/site/public/.gitkeep
/site/resources/
/site/static/en/images/
/site/static/da/images/
/site/static/fr/images/
/site/static/de_x_sie/images/
/site/.hugo_build.lock
